    "description": "[Unmarked]\nBrass-Tone Metal Double Inkwell Set\nVictorian Style, Mid-20th Century or Earlier\nThis ornate desk set features a central gnome or elf figure with a long beard and pointed cap, situated between two lidded inkwells. The base is heavily decorated with scrolling foliate motifs and includes a built-in pen tray at the front. The set reflects the whimsical and highly decorative Aesthetic and Victorian movements, often incorporating mythological or folklore figures into functional household items. The set is accompanied by a horse-head letter opener and a small spoon with a bust-handle finial.\nCast metal construction with a brass-tone finish and natural aged patina\nSet includes dual hinged-lid inkwells, one ceramic insert, horse-head letter opener, and bust-handle spoon\nDetailed gnome figure casting and ornate scrollwork base\nApproximate dimensions: 8\" wide x 6\" deep x 5.5\" high\nCondition:\nGood vintage condition with natural oxidation and patina consistent with age. One inkwell is missing its interior liner; the other contains a white ceramic liner with visible ink staining. Hinges are intact and functional. Letter opener and spoon show minor surface wear. No structural breaks or repairs visible.",
    "score_reasons": [
      "Shipping is calculated and not included in the price (-4)",
